    {
      "id": "0101-dark-slide-markdown-is-escaped",
      "title": "dark-slide: a value in markdown content is backslash-escaped",
      "since": "0.35.0",
      "tags": [
        "template",
        "profiles"
      ],
      "fn": "render",
      "input": {
        "template": {
          "fancyTemplate": 1,
          "writer": "dark-slide",
          "variables": {
            "name": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "logo": {
              "type": "image"
            },
            "url": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "document": {
            "slides": [
              {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "x": 0,
                    "y": 0,
                    "w": 1,
                    "h": 1,
                    "content": "Hello {{ name }}",
                    "format": "markdown"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "data": {
          "name": "*bold* _x_ # [a](javascript:x) `c` \\ 1. <b>&"
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "ok": true,
        "document": {
          "slides": [
            {
              "elements": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "x": 0,
                  "y": 0,
                  "w": 1,
                  "h": 1,
                  "content": "Hello \\*bold\\* \\_x\\_ \\# \\[a\\]\\(javascript\\:x\\) \\`c\\` \\\\ 1\\. \\<b\\>\\&",
                  "format": "markdown"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "notes": "THE NAMED MARKDOWN ROW. The value is never parsed as markup; the template's own `Hello ` is untouched. CommonMark escaping. dark-slide's PPTX MarkdownInline does not yet honour backslash escapes (SPEC 9).",
      "skip": {
        "php": "The dark-slide profile is phase 6 of the plan (TS + Python legs; holy-sheet and dark-slide profiles). The PHP leg implements fine-print and last-word only; this row is the spec it will be built against."
      }
    },
